From: K2B_RetroArch
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: arm64: load the kernel 2 MiB aligned

booti places an arm64 Image at a 2 MiB-aligned address. With kernel_addr_r
at DRAM + 512 KiB it decompresses the LZ4 kernel there and then moves the
whole 44.7 MB Image up to DRAM + 2 MiB: "Moving Image from 0x40080000 to
0x40200000", 0.30 s of every boot on the K2B (serial, host-timestamped).
Load at DRAM + 2 MiB and there is nothing to move. The decompressed Image
then ends at ~0x42f60000, still below kernel_comp_addr_r (DRAM + 64 MiB)
where booti keeps the compressed copy.

---
--- a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
+++ b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@
  * Scripts, PXE and DTBs should go afterwards, leaving the rest for the initrd.
  */
 #define BOOTM_SIZE        __stringify(0xa000000)
-#define KERNEL_ADDR_R     __stringify(SDRAM_OFFSET(0080000))
+#define KERNEL_ADDR_R     __stringify(SDRAM_OFFSET(0200000))
 #define KERNEL_COMP_ADDR_R __stringify(SDRAM_OFFSET(4000000))
 #define KERNEL_COMP_SIZE  __stringify(0xb000000)
 #define FDT_ADDR_R        __stringify(SDRAM_OFFSET(FA00000))
